Use the present perfect for an experience, a recent result, or an action that began in the past and remains connected with now. Do not use the present perfect with a finished time such as yesterday.', '[{"example":"I visited Da Nang last summer.","explanation":"Last summer gives a finished past time."},{"example":"I have visited Da Nang twice.","explanation":"The sentence describes experience without a finished time."}]', 'Avoid “I have visited it last year.” Use “I visited it last year.”', 20, 'original', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'Original Sprint 9 batch 1; editorial, answer, and provenance review completed 2026-09-12.', 'active', CURRENT_TIMESTAMP, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP FROM topics t WHERE t.slug='core-tenses' AND NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM grammar_lessons WHERE slug='past-simple-and-present-perfect');











